.TH PORTGLANCE 1 "October 2026" "PortGlance 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portglance \- see which dev servers are listening, at a glance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portglance
.RB [ \-\-background | \-\-widget | \-\-demo | \-\-quit ]
.br
.B portglance list
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-udp ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-docker ]
.br
.B portglance kill
.I PORT
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PortGlance
shows the TCP ports your development servers listen on, together with the
process, PID, uptime, memory use and the project each one belongs to (the git
repository containing the process' working directory). Docker and Podman
containers are listed with their published ports.
.PP
Without a subcommand, the graphical application starts, or the running
instance is brought to the front. It keeps running in the background with a
top-panel indicator showing the number of dev ports in use.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start with only the top-panel indicator. Used by the login autostart entry.
.TP
.B \-\-widget
Show the desktop widget.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start a few fake dev servers in throwaway projects and show them. Settings
and the autostart entry are not touched.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Print the dev ports as a table.
.B \-\-all
includes system ports,
.B \-\-udp
includes UDP sockets,
.B \-\-json
prints machine-readable output and
.B \-\-no\-docker
skips containers.
.TP
.BI kill " PORT"
Stop whatever listens on
.IR PORT .
Processes receive SIGTERM and, if they are still running after
.B \-\-timeout
seconds (default 5), SIGKILL.
.B \-\-force
sends SIGKILL straight away. Containers are stopped through the Docker or
Podman API. Asks for confirmation unless
.B \-\-yes
is given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/portglance/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.rafay_ah.PortGlance.desktop
Start-on-login entry, created on first run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ss (8),
.BR lsof (8),
.BR fuser (1)
.PP
https://github.com/rafay-ah/portglance
